# Engineering standards

## Change size

- One concern per change (budget path, loop breaker, docs — not all at once)
- Prefer the smallest diff that solves the problem; match nearby patterns
- Do not add abstractions, frameworks, or config knobs “for later”
- Keep `cmd/tokenguard` thin; put logic in `internal/*`

## Before you ship

1. Run `go test ./...` (and `go test ./test/... -count=1` if proxy/guard/e2e touched)
2. If you added an env var → update `.env.example`
3. If status codes, headers, or routes changed → update `docs/API.md` (+ `HOW_TO_USE.md` if operator-facing)
4. If pricing/models changed → prefer OpenRouter sync / mgmt upsert; do not grow `pricing.json` for every new model

## Safety defaults

- Fail closed in guarded mode (missing Turso/Redis → `503`, never pass-through)
- Money = `int64` micro-USD; no float ledger math
- Strip `X-TokenGuard-*` before upstream; never log plaintext `tg_` keys
- Unknown model → block (`400`); do not invent prices

## Local sanity

- Default listen is `:8080` (`.env`); smoke-test docs use `127.0.0.1:18080` only when that env is set
- Health check: `GET /healthz` → `{"status":"ok"}`
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, or `tokenguard.exe`
